Make document attachment on stock moves OBVIOUS and complete in one user flow.

Backend (StockService.java — surgical, 5 edits):
- MoveResponse +linkedDocCount (Integer) — eliminates N+1 in history page
- history() SQL +subquery: (select count(*) from stock_move_document where move_id = m.id)
- rowToMoveResponse reads linked_doc_count from the row
- toMoveResponse (JPA path) computes linkedDocCount via count query
- documentsOf() enriched: JOIN document + doc_folder → returns title, reference, docType
  alongside documentId + primary (was just {documentId, primary} → dialog showed UUIDs)

Frontend:
- document-picker-dialog.component.ts (NEW, 205 lines) — reusable picker scoped to
  the project's 05.01 BL folder only. Lists docs via DocumentService.search(folderId).
  Emits picked event with selected documentId.
- move-form.component.ts (10 edits):
  - Fixed docType bug: 'BL' → 'BON_LIVRAISON' (was rejected by backend as INVALID_PARAMETER)
  - Compensation toast for orphaned uploads (upload OK + postMove fail → explicit French message)
  - Project selector for CENTRAL-only IN moves (doc-folder requires projectId)
  - 'Ou choisir un document existant' link + picker integration (mutually exclusive with upload)
  - canAttachDocument() relaxed to allow CENTRAL IN with project selector
  - Blocks CENTRAL→CENTRAL TRANSFER (no project context)
- stock-moves.component.ts (10 edits):
  - 'Aucun justificatif' empty state (was bare em-dash)
  - 'Ajouter un justificatif' button in docs dialog (gated by STOCK_MOVE)
  - Removed N+1 preloadDocCounts() loop — uses m.linkedDocCount from enriched response
  - Picker wired → linkDocument() junction endpoint
- stock.model.ts: +linkedDocCount field + mapMove; mapLinkedDocument reads 'primary'

E2E: 5/5 PASS
- S13: IN + upload → doc in 05.01 BL + linked + enriched documentsOf (title/docType/primary)
- S14: IN without doc still works (optional attachment)
- S15: IDOR blocked — amel (BUREAU) linkDocument → HTTP 403 FORBIDDEN
- S16: CENTRAL IN requires project selector — doc-folder without projectId → 400; docType=BL → 400
- BONUS: linkedDocCount in history (no N+1) — all moves have the field via single SQL subquery

No backend contract changes. No cash/process/payment changes. No Part 2.
ng build: 0 errors. Backend compile: BUILD SUCCESS.
